{"name":"Love for All","hex":"#cd0106","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"},{"term":"for","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Fore."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["Because."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for"},{"term":"all","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Allar."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["Every individual or anything of the given class, with no exceptions (the noun or noun phrase denoting the class must be plural or uncountable).","Throughout the whole of (a stated period of time; generally used with units of a day or longer)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/1280px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_